{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_04dbdf3064d0ed53717683a7f0a82219cd60aa6cfa784828b043d71e90b14348","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_cb2f5d22f48bcbba69e238b7b10d690e1e5b503873aa830a2632cb74dd29b61b","slc_e66640011515384696214a9c3ebc193f0a6edd93ed603da28a429456f37c5417"],"source_ids":["src_768fbe73690e547b8ff3d5f281258758"],"text":"Grinta is described as a local-first coding agent built to finish long, failure-prone software tasks, released under the MIT license and maintained by Youssef Mejdi.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0ae662a46b21eab9245fb2812159d268190ef2c8c1db1bf48ff875b359490756","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4744951745aec46299e1f9762b2bb624bacf9bc9f632ce03117634f19687b655","slc_e7fb1a91a21552533574de4e041989bdbd237d72b3203c00098382adee25c907"],"source_ids":["src_c6dca1f4dafa573b93b4bc2d33154982"],"text":"Errors are classified as recoverable or terminal; recoverable errors retry with backoff, while terminal errors emit an error observation and transition to an ERROR state. Public lifecycle states include RUNNING, RETRYING, RATE_LIMITED, FINISHED, and others.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1099654794c6eea5d9cde50bc7321254a9cd8302496c5da94d7cba3849c53752","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9104091fb243dfe257c132c1d35184f9971b10c093548f7c1d031b5fdae023bd","slc_d6467f54ab3e2bc36168b80a42ee06974e54a1190453e8fab6d1fd81974120a5"],"source_ids":["src_768fbe73690e547b8ff3d5f281258758","src_c6dca1f4dafa573b93b4bc2d33154982"],"text":"The architecture has four layers: interface (launcher, TUI, non-interactive runner), orchestration (planning, retries, finish validation), execution (local commands, files, tools), and durability (event stream and persisted state).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_222d0bf6cd230f7fe798ed8f6fcc2f1d969ae90817f497cabe132ad021becac1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3b34be05e76628669dddea2a898b64557f13cfafb7ed3ffb1116c7dabfeebc54","slc_618c32fbf6cdf0b9458bdfa4f798ddf038bb5b128ca4f8b827872dd63ce5d2a5","slc_c35a6af53e5c8c9c939a3878b2bf52fe7df441304c7fddf152628e0d1356a34b","slc_ce38c4779240912cc1b1bd0cfad2ab62899cdf05924bfebc9ce8b5535bb95b16","slc_da2e99692520371a3cc8fe43985b6af8c410a263eed07324bd98e0dce43705dc"],"source_ids":["src_17fb0110fa3c593586e4d1f92a97c7ce","src_30b0a33412ec59169f0a5e31a984d184"],"text":"Repository development practice: the project follows a maintainer-led governance model with a single lead maintainer holding release and merge authority, and best-effort review targets of 5 business days for bugs and 7 for pull requests.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_310275175c08ec391624e5e55960d7e3bd01afe08009dc60debcbe1df68f534a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_79e0783d84acc8de344b13667f9d90d021a5d4c4d547f65af8a84d5848e42264","slc_a89c4d8358202143cef213795f1fcf07fc15e1169fea798599636608e38cdc52","slc_b4d325e377730df4d920b3f51b9fb1f6fdf299ed21ccb3e4bc26a295ae60546c"],"source_ids":["src_768fbe73690e547b8ff3d5f281258758","src_c6dca1f4dafa573b93b4bc2d33154982"],"text":"CLI subcommands include grinta init, grinta doctor, grinta sessions list/show/export/prune, and flags such as --project, --model, --theme, --minimal, --accessible, and --cleanup-storage.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_31ec52affa00f6538887dbaf8bc0196fcb029c46ba143b15e5eefdb097251ef8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_56565dba42abf7125214146d19a97bd9d54d5df9b4e8979074302fe43ffdb2a9","slc_7085d639777c972e24fb49f301f40ae0f85f476fcaffc58a1936c3874e73e718"],"source_ids":["src_768fbe73690e547b8ff3d5f281258758"],"text":"Grinta runs commands with the local user's privileges; confirmation prompts, secret masking, workspace boundaries, and process isolation reduce risk but do not make hostile code safe, and the docs recommend a VM or container for untrusted repositories.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_50fcd673989fdddb93625ad1a28efe99c2b4bc31e64122d28c774d638bfd504c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_15f86a5def9b7d6b7ad6759ee08d97fbdefe8e4a0a06375f33341a447ca54218","slc_37ebd0d798a64f8754cfc45a435623313ea0b6067f7da749645f09221c9d15f8","slc_7cfc0caa6abf85255fc4a26cc0a2f75b50f1a9b2c94e9d138442df463251ab39"],"source_ids":["src_768fbe73690e547b8ff3d5f281258758","src_c6dca1f4dafa573b93b4bc2d33154982"],"text":"A SessionOrchestrator coordinates focused services (retry, circuit breaker, stuck detection, task validation, state transitions) and runs actions through a middleware pipeline where safety checks execute first and telemetry last.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_62dd357b79cf35123c935e9a457f8ce1beccc7491cf8314bf89a0713281705a3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6a506634f35be2095d96c46b2811a60ef855c15234dfc4d99b950e8566395bcb","slc_c43e7c2a7d390701c864f04109953790b1e7e74663dc849f28020879f12fe885","slc_cae0c5a504d98264e32038dadfdae1e97be56724e6c387891826da04d2ec7d0e"],"source_ids":["src_768fbe73690e547b8ff3d5f281258758"],"text":"Inference supports OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, OpenRouter and other gateways, OpenAI-compatible endpoints, and local servers via Ollama, LM Studio, or vLLM; an optional rag extra provides semantic retrieval.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_72a8c1f7689632e9ce04b446bfe238777e5fc2f82e756f19f061df714c8cbd70","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_179dec4f6bc1d963ac3311005c269c58ec1c47dd7f30755c720f5ee4ca286168","slc_3fc13cbbd7471c04ef746aa9caa305ef0ffe3aadb5aa89555621d75d5f636790","slc_dd2ef0f02d6aaab3bf684c92f72429469f116fc5e37380a1cc2f2ba7da80f26e"],"source_ids":["src_768fbe73690e547b8ff3d5f281258758","src_c6dca1f4dafa573b93b4bc2d33154982"],"text":"The runtime targets Python 3.12 or 3.13, supports Linux, Windows, macOS, and WSL2, and the package metadata reports version 1.0.0.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_77148b411b4da0daa393e82964d948e18c9da30aa00ab5e782baac530a3c433e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7085d639777c972e24fb49f301f40ae0f85f476fcaffc58a1936c3874e73e718","slc_e6f02cbcddbfbe187086a18d3af464d7130a25058113fc5bfb95abe7141b5988"],"source_ids":["src_768fbe73690e547b8ff3d5f281258758","src_c6dca1f4dafa573b93b4bc2d33154982"],"text":"The sandboxed_local execution profile adds OS-native process-scoped isolation (bwrap, AppContainer, sandbox-exec) for supported non-interactive subprocess commands, but interactive PTY sessions stay outside that boundary and it is not a VM or host isolation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_779361263f7a1e553499ad22f825ad495ceffe2a90d1d5e896b3b6b93c2c3fd8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d6b37a17f2bae8723cd1ee9fa2301c9167c58b9b508ee4f816aa01df98f698ef"],"source_ids":["src_768fbe73690e547b8ff3d5f281258758"],"text":"The repository includes a headless adapter for the DeepSWE v1.1 benchmark that runs Grinta in an isolated task workspace, captures the patch and trajectory, and leaves pass/fail decisions to the benchmark verifier.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_79045bfc980a19397cbb57414993fee68a8dc3c38164ee897da41a368c9e7d31","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_179dec4f6bc1d963ac3311005c269c58ec1c47dd7f30755c720f5ee4ca286168","slc_58166f175364183423bbfefc69e15625007033155de7e394f36f742365af0b5a","slc_680175ecc44bf95eac2efd80b251118473c423604c50a61d3fc839eb5af8f66f","slc_7e41233fb26aaa5a8f634542e4d567456ceb8200e3a5c6940a1c474fd5371a36"],"source_ids":["src_768fbe73690e547b8ff3d5f281258758","src_c6dca1f4dafa573b93b4bc2d33154982"],"text":"The product offers a Textual terminal UI for TTY stdin and a non-interactive runner for piped input where each input line is one turn, plus slash commands like /mode, /model, /checkpoint, and /resume.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8ea3a48af0c2ba3540bf2ab8ac1ebe371ba550ba27570eaa758e21a7420f23fe","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2239126bfc7ad2ac1fa1392f5d78bf5bec6c824d4f35019287673d2e7dff6b65","slc_a06ae72efbfb033195e628e746c4bf910ea519e7e6ef877ba0ed7a6416bb6415"],"source_ids":["src_768fbe73690e547b8ff3d5f281258758"],"text":"Agent mode has three autonomy levels: conservative confirms shell commands, edits, MCP calls, and delegation; balanced (the default) confirms high-risk actions; full removes confirmation prompts while policy blocks still apply.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9bc3daf3960e3112634b1072f816832e7c8391bfaba41bdfdbab81126441518d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"josephsenior/grinta-coding-agent@918df240e0a5 snapshot 3ff10eff6d798156","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3f6eb0799bb153b99c392274866a6cc049842845a844d41022e995157f2fc1b6","slc_5356cc956988257637f4d12af88ce92673f7aec41d89cb192a486b048c5de4ff","slc_584a0c99a6e2790ae1151591fef2719e70b0394c81385db1bb7801a522f42464","slc_bffffebabe08b6d6cea0fde9848ce6ec7cb7432bbaa53695c4b6a7b527367337","slc_cc6e9959504be181109368491b6e154e1aa367c59d05e7e4d58e7221c8bc940f"],"source_ids":["src_768fbe73690e547b8ff3d5f281258758"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors clone the repo and run a platform setup script (start_here.sh or START_HERE.ps1 on Windows), then run pre-commit on all files and unit tests via PYTHONPATH=. uv run pytest backend/tests/unit before opening a pull request.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:08:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4d3ac37912724f7e9680b47bc67a1d0d"}
